Base 0ae1a692. Existing experimental voice/video setting also gates group voice, default off. Existing group, explicit join, one device per account where verified, up to four devices, direct host ICE and independent WebRTC legs. Coordinator owns admission while present. On leaving/timeout, established authorized legs may continue and joins stop; explicit end closes all. No durable signaling, relaying or group video.

1. Rust/Tauri authority: add a desktop command `group_voice_member(groupId, deviceId)` returning a verified account ID or null for current accepted device membership in the exact group (including current local device), fail closed for unknown/removed/pending or disabled calls/locked runtime. Reuse the exact signed projection and trusted identity/proof owner. Keep normal call signal IPC and its authenticated source unchanged. Add focused denial/current grant tests; frontend uses returned account for dedup.
2. Frontend: preserve direct calls, use existing runtime event ownership and experimental setting. Distinct group signaling envelope, one active group media session, hard cap incl pending joins, coordinator checked against exact group, explicit Join before capture. Bind meeting/roster and generation to authenticated source, use deterministic initiator per pair. Local shared mic, per-peer connection and remote audio sink, surfaced playback rejection, mute and leave, disable/lock/logout teardown; ensure stale callbacks cannot attach resources. Verify peers before SDP and close revoked legs on membership invalidation. Bound timeouts/retries only while active, no idle polling. Group entry from existing conversation; no media on post office.
3. Owning docs and validation.json: document experiment, control and media boundaries. Focused tests exercise disabled flag, invited/nonmember rejection, coordinator/capacity, no unsolicited capture, exact-meeting checks, signaling races and per-leg/session cleanup. Compose make verify-plan/verify-changed and standards-check. Native 2/3/4 endpoint, actual speaker overlap, playback errors, idle recovery and resource/latency limits need physical evidence.
